# pond/_util/intfloat — FRICTION

## DEPRECATED 2026-07-04 — surface superseded by std::math

`std::math::int_to_float` / `float_to_int` (upstream 2026-06-11)
and `std::math::round` / `trunc` (2026-06-14) cover this lib's
whole reason to exist. The lotus body now delegates to std::math
(the ASCII roundtrip through `parse_float(to_string(n))` is
gone) and the lib is marked deprecated in its README; kept as a
compatibility shim for vendored consumers. Zero in-tree
consumers remain. Removal is a future major-cut decision —
flagged for the root catalog.

The underlying language gap this lib papered over is NOT closed:
`let f: Float = i;` and `0.0 + n` widening still reject
(retested 2026-07-04 at hale 400ac68; see
§ pond/ml/neural "int-to-float-ascription-rejected").

