# pond/math/matrix — FRICTION

**2026-06-12 sweep (hale HEAD `43300e5`):** the lib's surface
matches CONTRACTS.md (as re-cut 2026-06-08 for the m90 CQRS
rule). The stale piece was the *examples*: `matmul-demo` (and
`math/stats`'s internals + `stats-demo`) still called the
retired `Mat` methods (`mx.from_rows(...)`, `mx.zeros(...)`,
`a.transpose()`), which typecheck against the empty `Mat` lotus
but die at codegen (`locus __lib_matrix_matrix_Mat has no
method from_rows`). Migrated to the free-fn surface
(`mat::from_rows(...)`, `mat::transpose(a)`); both demos build
and pass all checks at HEAD.

## Contract status

### Free-fn factories + sentinel pairs — [MATCHES CONTRACT]

History, shortest version:

1. **v1:** free fns couldn't return `LocusRef`, so factories
   lived as methods on a `Mat` namespace lotus; the (old)
   two-channel rule blocked `fallible(E)` on methods, so the
   binary ops shipped sentinel pairs (`error_matrix()` /
   `is_error`, `nan_sentinel()` / `is_nan`).
2. **hale v0.8.2 m90** inverted the first wall *permanently*
   (CQRS rule, not a codegen-v0 gap): methods may NOT return
   locus values; free fns MAY. Commit `04657b1` extracted all
   factories / binary ops / `transpose` to free fns; `Mat`
   remains an empty vestigial namespace lotus for source compat.
3. **CONTRACTS.md was re-cut 2026-06-08** to bless exactly this
   shape — free fns + sentinel-predicate pairs + fallible
   `_checked` accessors. The earlier "[CLOSABLE] flip matmul /
   add / dot / at / set_at to `fallible(E)`" notes are
   SUPERSEDED: the contract now specifies the sentinel shape,
   so no flip is pending. (Locus member fns CAN carry
   `fallible(E)` post-v0.8.1; the contract simply doesn't ask
   these to.)

`at` / `set_at` stay infallible with OOB sentinels per the
contract; `at_checked` / `set_at_checked` / `index_of` carry
the `fallible(IndexError)` surface as free fns.

## Language / stdlib gaps

### No `from-offset` `index_of` on strings — [still open, re-checked 2026-06-12]

`std::str` still has no `index_of_from(s, needle, start)` (the
builtin list has only `index_of`). `from_rows` keeps its manual
forward scan.

### NaN literal awkward — [CLOSED 2026-06-12]

`std::math::nan()` / `std::math::is_nan(f)` / `std::math::inf()`
now exist upstream — exactly the ask. `nan_sentinel()` and
`is_nan()` remain on the lib's contract surface but their bodies
delegate to std::math; the hand-rolled `0.0 / 0.0` and `f != f`
idioms are retired. (matmul-demo's NaN-sentinel check passes.)

### Float-from-Int literal mixing — [CLOSED 2026-06-12]

`std::math::int_to_float(i)` / `float_to_int(f)` now lower.
This lib had no widening hacks of its own; `pond/math/stats`
carried the `(0.0 + n)` idiom and migrated (see its FRICTION).

## Duplicate-suspected helpers

- **`is_nan` / `nan_sentinel`** — resolved upstream; the lib
  fns are now one-line delegates kept only for contract-surface
  stability.
- **`error_matrix()` / `is_error(m)` sentinel-pair pattern** —
  still pond-local. If another lib hits a "non-fallible op needs
  a typed-ish failure signal" shape it will reach for the same
  pattern; candidate for a pond-internal convention note rather
  than code sharing.

## Non-friction observations

- `@form(vec)` over `Float` cells worked first try; the
  synthesized `push` / `get` / `set` / `len` / `sort` covers the
  row-major buffer story.
- `or discard` remains the right addressing shape for the
  ignore-OOB `set` calls.

## unbounded-alloc triage — 2026-08-03 (first recorded)

Four default-on warnings at hale v0.13.0, all vec-inserts in
the buffer-fill loops of `zeros`, `transpose`, and `from_rows`
(×2). TRUE-but-by-design: each loop fills a freshly-constructed
Matrix to exactly `rows * cols` cells — the allocation IS the
factory's contract, bounded by the caller-requested dimensions.
Same verdict class as embeddings' `Store::add`. No source
change.


