## 11. NEW (2026-06-12): `sqlite::Db` cannot satisfy `db::DbDriver` — resolved with the `SqliteDriver` adapter (F.7 counterpart)

**The conflict.** CONTRACTS.md § pond/migrations annotates
`driver: db::DbDriver` with "injected: pq::PgConn / pq::PgPool /
sqlite::Db". But the locked § pond/sqlite surface (now implemented
for real) is the fallible-method shape — `exec(sql) -> ExecResult
fallible(DbError)` with sqlite-local result types — which is
signature-incompatible with the interface's non-fallible
`ok`/`err`-packed `db::*` shapes, and is missing the interface's
lifecycle/params/txn methods entirely. One locus can't carry both
`exec` signatures. Logged on the sqlite side as
`FRICTION.log § F.7`; this entry is the consumer-side
counterpart and the shipped resolution.

**Resolution (option (a) from F.7).** This lib ships
`sqlite_driver.hl`: `locus SqliteDriver { params { conn:
sqlite::Db; ... } }` — a thin adapter that catches every DbError
on the value channel and repacks it into the `db::*` result
shapes, structurally satisfying the FULL `db::DbDriver` method
set (backend/open/close/exec/query_one/query_all/exec_params/
query_params/begin/commit/rollback/tx_status). The `Migrator`
surface stays CONTRACTS.md-verbatim; injection reads

```hale
let conn = sqlite::Db { path: ... };
let m = migs::Migrator { driver: migs::SqliteDriver { conn: conn } };
```

**Proposed CONTRACTS.md amendment.** In § pond/migrations, change
the injectable comment from "… / sqlite::Db" to "… /
migs::SqliteDriver (adapter over sqlite::Db — sqlite::Db itself
does not satisfy the interface, see sqlite F.7)". The § pond/sqlite
status blockquote ("migrating onto the db::DbDriver method set is
part of the F.1 unblock pass") should drop that clause — the F.1
pass landed and deliberately kept the fallible-method contract
shape instead.

**Placement — CLOSED 2026-07-06 (promoted to pond/sqlite).** The
adapter moved to its natural home as `sqlite::Driver`
(`sqlite/driver.hl`, verbatim logic; locus renamed to drop the
seed-name stutter), mirroring how pq::PgConn carries its own
translation. CONTRACTS.md § pond/sqlite gained the `Driver` block
+ status note. Consequences here: this lib imports ONLY `../db`
now (pure Hale — `hale test migrations/` needs no @ffi link
shims), and `tests/sqlite_driver_test.hl` moved to
`sqlite/tests/driver_test.hl`.

---

## 12. NEW (2026-06-12): `import "vendor/pond/db"` resolved nothing in-tree — and `hale check` didn't notice

The 2026-05-29 rewrite imported the driver interface as
