# pond/router — friction log

Format borrows from `notes/hale-friction.md` upstream: one
entry per gap, date-stamped, with the smallest reproducer that
forced the call.

**2026-06-12 sweep (hale HEAD `43300e5`):** the three gated
restorations from the upstream post-audit note all verified
lifted by /tmp probes and were applied — `use(m)` is a Router
method again, the route table is one `RouteEntry` vec, and
`Context` carries `req: std::http::Request`. Closed entries are
kept below with their evidence; the live entries are
`url-decoding` and the `or raise` code-shape note.

---

## 2026-05-16 — use-is-reserved

**Status:** [CLOSED 2026-06-12]

`use` parses as a locus-method name at HEAD — probe
(`locus R { fn use(m: Int) -> Int { ... } }` + `r.use(1)`)
builds and runs. (Free-fn position was never re-tested because
the contract names it as a method; note `fn run(...)` at free-fn
position DOES still parse-fail, so lifecycle keywords are not
generally unreserved.) `Router.use(m: Middleware)` is restored
per CONTRACTS.md; the `use_mw` / `use_before` / `use_after`
free-fn shims are retired.

*Historical (2026-05-16):* `use` was treated as
future-reserved; the lib shipped `use_mw(before, after)` and
later `use_mw(m)`.

---

## 2026-05-16 — context-req-field

**Status:** [CLOSED 2026-06-12]

`type Ctx { r: std::http::Request; tag: String; }` builds and
runs at HEAD — the pass-A0 ordering rejection ("declared in
stdlib path-renames table but not registered in user_loci ...")
is gone. `Context` is restored to the contract shape:

```hale
type Context { req: std::http::Request; params: RouteParams; }
```

Handlers read `ctx.req.method` / `ctx.req.path` /
`ctx.req.headers` / `ctx.req.body`. Note `ctx.req.path` is the
RAW request target (query string included); the dispatcher
strips it for matching and `ctx.params.qs` carries the query
half. The 2026-05-16 flattened Context (method/path/headers/
body copied into Context) is retired.

---

## 2026-05-16 — response-in-fn-ptr-field

**Status:** [GATE-LIFTED — local type KEPT by choice, 2026-06-12]

The same pass-A0 fix means `handler: fn(Context) ->
std::http::Response` fields (and std-typed fields generally)
now resolve. The local `router::Response` is nonetheless
retained: Hale has no type-alias/re-export surface, so
"collapsing" it means handler authors write
`std::http::Response` literals — a consumer-facing signature
break with no ergonomic win over the field-equal local type +
one boundary copy in `__router_to_http`. Revisit only if a
consumer needs std-Response-specific machinery inside handlers.

2026-06-12 addendum: `std::http::Response` gained a
`headers: String` field upstream (C11); `router::Response`
mirrors it and `__router_to_http` passes it through, closing
the old "header-parsing" gap below.

