## upstream CLI gap: `hale test` cannot link `@ffi` libs — CLOSED 2026-07-18 (upstream fix)

`hale test`'s per-file compile (`compile_test_binary`,
hale-cli main.rs:1137) calls `build_executable_with_imports`
directly and never runs the Stage-2 `collect_ffi_from_imports`
pickup that `hale build` does (main.rs ~1817) — so every test
importing this lib (sqlite's own tests, jobs', migrations')
fails at link with `undefined reference to lotus_sqlite_*`,
regardless of the C_INCLUDE_PATH/LIBRARY_PATH shims. The tests
themselves are fine.

Interim gate (documented in each affected test header and in
CLAUDE.md § Build & verify): build each test as a binary and
run it —

    C_INCLUDE_PATH=$HOME/.local/include LIBRARY_PATH=$HOME/.local/lib \
      hale build <lib>/tests/<x>_test.hl && ./<lib>/tests/<x>_test

Pass = exit 0 + silent, same contract the runner enforces. All
five ffi-linking tests pass this gate (2× runs, re-runnable).
`.gitignore` gained the `**/tests/**` extensionless rule so the
interim binaries can't be committed. Upstream ask: run the same
ffi pickup in the test compile path; then this entry closes and
`hale test .` goes fully green (currently 43 passed / 5
ffi-link failures, all this class).

CLOSED 2026-07-18: upstream shipped exactly that —
`compile_test_binary` now runs `collect_ffi_from_imports` and
builds with the ffi options (hale > v0.11.8). Verified here:
`hale test sqlite/` 3/3, `hale test jobs/` 1/1,
`hale test migrations/` 1/1, all green with only the
C_INCLUDE_PATH/LIBRARY_PATH shims — no manual build gate. The
interim per-test `hale build` workaround is obsolete.

